        bodyEn = "Under Sarduri II, who ruled about 764–735 BC, Urartu reached the peak of its power. He called himself 'king of the universe' in imitation of Assyrian titles and campaigned widely, from the Euphrates to the Caspian. New fortresses and canals were built, and the capital Tushpa was enlarged. But Assyria regained its strength under Tiglath-Pileser III, and in 743 BC the Urartian-led coalition was crushed in northern Syria. In 735 BC the Assyrians invaded Urartu itself; Sarduri was defeated and shut himself up in Tushpa. The kingdom survived, but the long decline had begun. Sarduri's reign is thus both the golden age and the turning point of Urartu.",
